    {
      "title": "Delhi protests: Six police personnel injured as 1,000 protesters detained",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/delhi-protests-six-police-personnel-injured-as-1-000-protesters-detained-126101000719_1.html",
      "description": "Six Delhi Police personnel, including a female member of the Pink Force, sustained injuries during the detention of around 1,000 protesters in different parts of New Delhi district on Saturday, with instances of stones being hurled at the security personnel at at least two places, an officer said.\nThe injured personnel were rushed to nearby hospitals for treatment, the officer said, adding that the circumstances in which they were injured are being ascertained.\nSuman, a member of the Pink Force, told PTI that her finger got fractured while she was detaining protesters near the Hanuman temple at Commaught Place.\n\"A protest was taking place near the Hanuman temple, where a crowd of around 100 to 150 people had gathered. We detained the protesters, during which some women twisted my finger, resulting in a fracture,\" she said.\nShe added that the women were detained. \"But I cannot identify who specifically twisted my finger as it is difficult to pinpoint an individual in a large crowd.",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-10T15:07:47"
    },
    {
      "title": "One Delhi, many Jantar Mantars as protesters hit streets across the city",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/one-delhi-many-jantar-mantars-as-protesters-hit-streets-across-the-city-126101000759_1.html",
      "description": "With Jantar Mantar out of reach, CJP protesters scattered across Delhi as police detained 3,000 people, including several prominent leaders and public figures",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-10T13:40:16"
    },
    {
      "title": "CJP protest: Over 7,000 detained as Delhi Police cracks down on protesters",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/cjp-protest-over-3-000-detained-as-delhi-police-tightens-security-126101000584_1.html",
      "description": "Delhi Police on Saturday detained more than 3,000 protesters, who were trying to reach Jantar Mantar for the proposed CJP stir against Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar.\nSources said the protesters were detained across the New Delhi area and other districts, where police are using drones to monitor movement of people attempting to reach the protest site.\nThe protesters were detained from several places, including near Regal Cinema, Minto Bridge and near Akashwani Bhawan.\nAhead of the Cockroach Janta Party's (CJP) proposed protest at Jantar Mantar, police sources said over 600 people with criminal records were also detained across all the districts of the national capital as part of preventive measures.\nThe preventive action is aimed at ensuring that people with criminal backgrounds do not create a law-and-order situation during the proposed demonstration, the sources said.\nPolice are also keeping a close watch on the movements of certain people, who could mobilise crowds o",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-10T12:26:02"
    },
    {
      "title": "Over 500 detained, 2 cops injured in stone-pelting near Akashwani Bhawan",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/over-500-detained-2-cops-injured-in-stone-pelting-near-akashwani-bhawan-126101000368_1.html",
      "description": "Protesters allegedly stone-pelted security personnel at Imtiaz Ali Marg near Akashwani Bhawan after toppling barricades during the proposed Cockroach Janata Party (CJP) stir against Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar in the national capital on Saturday, officials said.\nAround noon, 25 to 30 protesters jumped barricades on Imtiaz Ali Marg and stone-pelleted at security personnel, they said, adding that some of them have been detained and two police personnel were injured in the process.\nPolice have detained about 500 people as protesters attempted to reach Jantar Mantar despite authorities denying permission to protest and enforcing strict security measures across the New Delhi district. Several protesters were chased and detained as they tried to regroup at different locations and evade the security cordon.\nThe protest was scheduled to begin at 10.30 am, but police and paramilitary personnel prevented participants from reaching the designated area, where prohibitory orders ar",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-10T08:34:49"
    }
  ]
